reviews.body:
Thanks. As written this can't merge, because it's what #712 asked not to do. `crates/gpu/Cargo.toml` drops wgpu's `metal`, `dx12` and `gles` features, egui-wgpu loses its defaults, and `select::backends()` returns Vulkan only. The consequences:
- stock macOS (no MoltenVK) can't open the app;
- Windows loses DX12 and WARP (#633's test VM rendered on "Microsoft Basic Render Driver (Dx12)");
- Linux loses the GL fallback.

The AGENTS.md, ROADMAP.md and ADR edits also record a "Vulkan only" decision that wasn't made.

What's wanted, per the maintainer's comment on #712 (2026-10-24):
- the GPU backend is **user-configurable** (a setting, plus the existing `WGPU_BACKEND`/`FIELDCRAFT_GPU` overrides);
- **defaults:** Vulkan on Linux and Windows, Metal on macOS, which must work out of the box without MoltenVK;
- unsupported backends show as **"coming soon"** in that setting, not removed;
- **no silent exit:** when the chosen backend has no adapter, the app says so visibly and falls back where it can.

Could you rework it along those lines, dropping the rules and ADR edits? It also conflicts with develop: `docs/lbm-collision.md` and `docs/lbm-gpu-performance.md` were moved under `docs/manual/` (ca35e80f).
